I’ve been getting a lot of questions lately about whether this recent broadening will give equal weight a lift, with many not realizing that both equal weight and small caps have outperformed S&P 500 for past year … also, not all growth (or value) indexes are created equal, so when someone mentions how “growth stocks” (or “value stocks”) are doing you need to know how they’re defining those from an index perspective
@Bloomberg 
[Past performance is no guarantee of future results]

One of the more important things to remember is bear markets don't just start and pull everything lower.

@sonusvarghese looked at the tech bust and found the S&P 500 fell 11% from April to December 2000, yet low volatility stocks soared 32%.

For more than two years now we've had exposure to both low vol and momentum names in the models we run.

